# Feature tests (always on)

A new feature is unfinished until its tests land in the **same step** as the code.

## Required

1. **Same PR / step.** Feature code and tests ship together. No "tests next" deferral.
2. **Behavior, not internals.** Assert what a caller or user can observe (HTTP status/body, DB outcome, refused work, match reasons). Prefer MVP.md acceptance IDs (`T29`, `T30`, …) when the feature maps to one.
3. **pytest in `tests/`.** Follow existing fixtures (`conftest.py`, `migrated_engine`, session, client). Name the file after the feature (`tests/test_<area>.py`).
4. **Run before done.** `pytest` for the touched tests (or the suite) must pass before commit, push, PR, or "step complete".
5. **Gate the step.** If the feature has no observable behavior worth asserting, it is too vague — shrink scope or drop it.

## Not required

- Pure docs / MVP decision rows (D-rows)
- Comment-only or typo fixes
- Throwaway spikes when the user explicitly says skip tests (state that in the step report)

## Anti-patterns

```text
❌ Ship app/foo.py now; "add tests later"
❌ Only mock the unit under test so the test can't fail
❌ Assert private helpers / call counts instead of outcomes
✅ One test that fails if the feature is removed or broken
```
